13 Mar 26
Order of 2 mod p
Note when \ord_p(2)=p-1 then 2 is a primitive root of p
If q is a factor of Mersenne number M_p then 2 is not a primitive
root of q.  The order of 2 mod q is p.  This includes the
situation where the Mersenne number M_p is a prime
A different observation is that primes p that have order of 2 mod
p = n can be found in the prime factors of 2^n-1

